    "chunk_size_bytes": 1296,
    "chunk_text": "The section \"ethical\" particularly stated, \"....aims to build trust in the systems by ensuring integrity...\" It was a brief section which described it. I wish the Government had a far more comprehensive programme put up on the website. At least that sentence seemed a little bit wider, reflecting the mandate that the Government got at the last\n\n961 962\n\n\u0db4\u0ddc\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0db8\u0dc1\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4 \u0dc0\n\napplicability and that the police will misuse it; they will always misuse it. That has been the history of this terrible law. And, even if your Government wishes to be otherwise, the law is applied by the police and they continue to misuse it and that is my point. So, you cannot have a policy saying that you want to be ethical and then backtrack from your previous position. Actually, that empowers a police which wants to be in transition. That is the point I am trying to make. The PTA is now being applied to teachers in schools! Yesterday, the TID had gone and questioned the teachers in Konavil Maha Vidyalayam in Kilinochchi. The TID in Paranthan had gone and questioned them because at a function, at a sports meet, there were certain artistic interpretations that the teachers had done and they have been questioned by the TID under the PTA. So, surely, there must be something done for this."
