    "chunk_text": "I will conclude by just saying this. The Hon. Prime Minister is now the Hon. Minister of Education, Higher Education and Vocational Education. When she was seated in the Opposition - actually she sat just behind me - she raised an issue with regard to the Jaffna Central College. In the Jaffna Central College, there was a new lady principal who was appointed and she was fully qualified. She was from the Sri Lanka Principals\u2019 Service. But, because of political interference by Douglas\n\n963 964\n\n[\u0db8\u0db1\u0dca \u0da2\u0dd3.\u0da2\u0dd3. \u0dc1\u0db4\u0ddc\u0dca \u0db1\u0db6\u0d9a\u0db1 \u0dab\u0dc4\u0dad\u0ddc]\n\n2025 \u0da2\u0dca\u200d \u0dc0\u0ddc\u0dd2\u0db4 22\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd2\u0dc0\u0dba\u0ddd\u0da2\u0dba \u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0d9a \u0dc3\u0dcf\u0db7\u0dcf\u0db4\u0dad\u0dd2\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0dd2\u0dba\u0dba (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b95\u0bc1\u0bb4\u0bc1\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bcd \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bcd \u0ba4\u0bb5\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bbe\u0bb3\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Deputy Chairperson of Committees) \u0dd9\u0dd0\u0dca \u0dcf\u0ddc\u0dc0 \u0d85\u0dc0\u0d82\u0dca \u0dbb\u0dca , \u0db8\u0db1\u0dca \u0dab\u0dca\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd4 \u0dab\u0db1\u0dd2.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0da2\u0dd3.\u0da2\u0dd3. \u0dc0\u0db4\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dca\u0db1\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0dbd\u0db8\u0dca \u0dd9\u0dad\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9c\u0bc0.\u0b9c\u0bc0. \u0ba4\u0baa\u0bbe\u0ba9\u0bcd\u0ba9\u0bae\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bb2\u0bae\u0bcd) (The Hon. G.G. Ponnambalam) One last thing, Madam, with regard to solar power. For over three or four months, solar meters are not being issued by the CEB. There are people who have spent millions of rupees on solar power; because of the increasing rise in the prices of electricity, they have invested in millions. But, because the CEB is not issuing solar meters, they are at a complete loss. They have spent money, but they are not able to get the benefit of that investment. At least now, the Government must look into that. These are uncontroversial issues.\n\nAlso, look at the issues of the PTA, memorialization and the political prisoners. My good Friend, the Hon. Minister of Justice has said that there are no political prisoners. The JVP identifies their former prisoners as political prisoners. The President at speeches in Jaffna had said political prisoners will have to be released and since he is committed to that position, he must look into that. Thank you."
