    "chunk_text": "\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dda\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0dc1\u0db8\u0dca\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4\u0dab \u0db1\u0dd2\u0dc0\u0dba\u0ddd\u0da2\u0dba \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bcd \u0b9a\u0baa\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Deputy Speaker) Order, please! Hon. Member, could you please stick to the Votes of Condolence? Please, stick to the topic.\n\n[11.20 a.m.] \u0d9c\u0dd4\u0dab \u0d9a\u0db6\u0dd3\u0dbb\u0dca \u0dad\u0dc2\u0dd3\u0dda \u0db8\u0dad\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b95\u0baa\u0bc0\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0bb9\u0bb7\u0bc0\u0bae\u0bcd) (The Hon. Kabir Hashim) Hon. Deputy Speaker, today, I would like to express my condolences to the families of all four Hon. Members who had passed away.\n\nThe late Hon. Rukman Senanayake, who was 76 years old when he passed away, was the grandson of the first Prime Minister of Sri Lanka, the late Hon. D.S. Senanayake. Though he was born to a powerful political family, he cut his own teeth in politics. At that time, he was a rebel in politics and was also a strong, dedicated member of the United National Party, the UNP. He also served the people diligently during his period as a politician.\n\nSir, the late Hon. Rukman Senanayake was from my District. He last contested from my District, Kegalle. He was elected twice as a Member of Parliament from the Kegalle District. In 1970s, at a by-election, he was first elected to Parliament. I remember - I was a young school boy at that time - that my father worked for that election and there was a lot of violence at that election. I can remember that my father\u2019s car was damaged badly at that election. But, the Hon.Rukman Senanayake, despite all the odds and with all the violence, emerged victorious and was elected to Parliament. Again in 2001, the Hon. Rukman Senanayake was elected from the Kegalle District and was our district leader. He gave leadership to\n\nthe Kegalle District for the United National Party. He was a very good leader and worked with everybody together. He was actually instrumental in bringing the open zoo concept into the Kegalle District."
  },
