    "chunk_text": "the Kegalle District for the United National Party. He was a very good leader and worked with everybody together. He was actually instrumental in bringing the open zoo concept into the Kegalle District.\n\nSir, I was fortunate to attend his funeral and to condole with his family and relatives. We, not only in Kegalle but all over the Island, respect him. At this time, I would like to convey my condolences to the Hon. Ruwan Wijewardene and Hon. Vasantha Senanayake, the extended members of his family. May he rest in peace!\n\nI would also like to say a few words about the late Hon. Sirinal de Mel. At the time when the late Hon. J.R. Jayewardene was the leader of the United National Party and President of Sri Lanka, people classified the United National Party as a capitalist party. It was the Hon. J.R. Jayewardene who started the unions, the Jathika Sevaka Sangamaya and the Lanka Jathika Wathu Kamkaru Sangamaya, under the UNP and gave representation to the working class within the UNP. He believed that the UNP could represent all the classes in this country. And, the late Hon.Sirinal de Mel was appointed as the head of the Jathika Sevaka Sangamaya. He, the Hon. Sirinal de Mel, was a legend. For years, he led the JSS successfully. Today, Mr. Gayan de Mel is here in the Speaker's Gallery. I would like to convey my condolences to him and the family. I would like to remind the yeoman service the late Hon. Sirinal de Mel rendered to the JSS and to the UNP. May he rest in peace!\n\nThen, I would like to speak about the late Hon. A. A. Reginald Perera, whom I did not know very closely, but I was in Parliament when he was here; he was a senior Parliamentarian. What I know is that in the Gampaha District, he was loved by the people, a politician that people loved. At this time, I console with the family and extend my condolences to them."
  },
