    "chunk_size_bytes": 1564,
    "chunk_text": "A classic example of that phenomenon is how the military has been involved in building this illegal Thissa Viharaya in Thyiddi. When we heard that the Army Commander at that time had come and laid the foundation stone and that it was being built on a private land, at the DCC meeting, within a few days of that foundation stone being laid, the matter had been discussed with the GA, the\n\nOn the 18th of December, 2024 when I first brought this up under this new Parliament, Madam, the All Ceylon Buddhist Congress had written a letter and its President or Chairman, Chandra Nimal Wakishta, has purportedly signed it. Madam, I table* that letter today.\n\nThis whole story is carried in today\u2019s \u201cUdayan\u201d newspaper. In the letter, they had claimed and insisted that that entire land of six acres, which is actually a privately deed land or privately-owned land, cannot be taken back and handed over to the people, that from King Devanampiyathissa's time, that land has belonged to the Thissa Viharaya and that, in fact, there should be, in total, 14 acres. So, an additional several acres have to be confiscated and given for the purposes of this viharaya. Madam, this is exactly what I meant by the military being a racist institution and that it has not changed its mindset. Even if we are to assume that there is some truth to these claims, there is a legal process by which you must go.\n\nJust because you are the military, you cannot decide that you can breach any law; the days of the law of the jungle is over. But, still, they are operating on that basis."
