    "chunk_size_bytes": 2322,
    "chunk_text": "it. When they could have easily built it on that land, which is rightfully owned by the viharaya, their choosing to confiscate privately owned land for this illegal act is something that cannot be allowed.\n\nThese matters should be discussed with Tamil Parliamentarians from Jaffna; we also have opinions. I mean, if you are actually going to build a much more capable international airport, actually Jaffna is the wrong place; it is in a corner. You can build it somewhere in the Vanni or Vavuniya, where you can serve Anuradhapura and the East since it is a much more central area. You do not go and build it in some corner. So, these are matters that have to be discussed and the Government must not take unilateral action, as reported in the newspapers.\n\nMadam, there is one other matter. The Land Reform Commission has an office in every district, outside the North and the East. In every district, outside the North and the East, there are 17 offices. In the North, there are five districts, but there is only one office in Jaffna and for Batticaloa and Trincomalee in the East, there is only one office in Batticaloa. But, in Ampara District, which has just less than 500 acres of land that comes within the LRC, has an office. Why is that? Should there not be an office in every district in the North and the East? Why is it that there are only two offices in areas that are predominantly Tamil-speaking? Is there not something wrong with that? We are complaining that lands are being stolen from us, that lands are being illegally taken away from us and it is the LRC which is the primary culprit. Why is it that, deliberately, an office is not being operated in each district in the North and the East?\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd2\u0db4\u0dba\u0ddd\u0da2\u200d \u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0d9a \u0dca\u0dc0\u0dcf\u0db4\u0dd2\u0db1\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0db8\u0dd2\u0dba (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b95\u0bc1\u0bb4\u0bc1\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bcd \u0bc6\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bcd \u0ba4\u0bb5\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0bb3\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Deputy Chairperson of Committees) \u0db6\u0db6\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dc0\u0dcf\u0da7 \u0db1\u0dd2\u0dba\u0db8\u0dd2\u0dad \u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbd\u0dba \u0d85\u0dc0\u0dc3\u0db1\u0dca \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0dc0\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dc0\u0dcf. \u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0da2\u0dd3.\u0da2\u0dd3. \u0db4\u0db4\u0ddc\u0dca\u0daf\u0db1\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0dbd\u0db8\u0dca \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dc3\u0dad\u0dca\u0dcf (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9c\u0bc0.\u0b9c\u0bc0. \u0ba4\u0bc6\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba9\u0bcd\u0ba9\u0bae\u0bcd\u0bc6\u0bb2\u0bae\u0bcd) (The Hon. G.G. Ponnambalam) I am winding up, Madan."
