    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "2c40d8f947414b0cf32b9a8c4c1aa0c5",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1722,
    "chunk_text": "Sir, I do not normally speak out of turn. But, since the Hon. Prime Minister is present here, I wish to seek a clarification and an answer, if possible, with regard to something that is of significant public concern. Hon. Prime Minister, I am pretty sure that you are aware that Mr. Lasantha Wickrematunge's daughter has written a letter to you. I have a copy of that letter and it is quite a damning letter. It calls for the Impeachment of the Attorney-General for gross abuse of power and gross neglect of duty. It is a four-page letter and the matters she raises in it are actually quite shocking. I think your Government has repeatedly come on record saying that the Attorney-General\u2019s Department is an independent institution and that there should be no interference with regard to decisions being made by it. But here, when a victim\u2019s family is actually casting aspersions on the very Head of that institution, with regard to that individual\u2019s conduct, I think it is a very important instance where the Government must in some way intervene. Since this letter is addressed to you and also copied to the Minister of Justice and National Integration, I wish to find out whether the Hon. Prime Minister has something in mind with regard to this matter. Thank you very much.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0dc0\u0d86\u0da0\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dba) \u0dc4\u0dbb\u0dd2\u0db1\u0dd2 \u0d85\u0db8\u0dbb\u0dc3\u0dd6\u0dbb\u0dd2\u0dba \u0db4\u0db8\u0db4\u0db1\u0dc0\u0dd2\u0dba (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 (\u0b95\u0bb2\u0bbe\u0bc7\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bbf) (\u0ba4\u0b9a\u0bb2\u0bcd\u0bb5\u0bbf) \u0bb9\u0bbe\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bbf \u0b85\u0bae\u0bb0\u0b9a\u0bc2\u0bbe\u0bbf\u0baf) (The Hon. (Dr.) (Ms.) Harini Amarasuriya) Thank you, Hon. Deputy Speaker.\n\nYes, Hon. Member, I have received the letter and I am planning to respond to that letter, to Ms. Wickrematunge, personally since she has sent it to me."
  },
  {
