    "md5": "bf962d3bc7b6143f734caf691a23fe77",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1821,
    "chunk_text": "12. Calls upon the Government of Sri Lanka to ensure the prompt, thorough and impartial investigation and, if warranted, prosecution of all alleged crimes relating to human rights violations ... with the full participation of victims and their representatives;\"\n\nWith this in mind, I have posed a few questions earlier to the Hon. Minister of Health regarding some details I sought.\n\nNumber two is, Interim Guidance on water, sanitation, hygiene and waste management for the COVID-19 virus dated 19th March, 2020 issued by the WHO and the UNICEF. This Interim Guidance still stands and has not been revised. Number three is, \"Statement on COVID 19: Ethical Considerations from a Global Perspective\", Statement of the UNESCO International Bioethics Committee and the UNESCO World Commission on the Ethics of Scientific Knowledge and Technology dated 26th March, 2020. This Guidance Statement still stands and has not been revised. Number four is, Recommended Measures for the Safe Burial of Bodies of Deceased Persons with COVID-19- Professional Working Group for the safe burial of bodies of deceased persons with COVID-19 in Sri Lanka. It details the hydrogeological factors in Sri Lanka in relation to disposal of COVID dead and was prepared by a group of Sri Lankan hydrogeologists and environmental engineers who\n\nprovide details of safe options for burial in Sri Lanka. Number five is, International Committee of the Red Cross: General Guidance for the management of the dead related to COVID -19 dated 31st March, 2020. This Interim Guidance still stands and has not been revised. Number six is, practical considerations and recommendations for religious leaders and faith-based communities in the context of COVID-19. That Interim Guidance dated 7th April, 2020 was issued by the WHO and has also not been revised."
