    "chunk_size_bytes": 1381,
    "chunk_text": "provide details of safe options for burial in Sri Lanka. Number five is, International Committee of the Red Cross: General Guidance for the management of the dead related to COVID -19 dated 31st March, 2020. This Interim Guidance still stands and has not been revised. Number six is, practical considerations and recommendations for religious leaders and faith-based communities in the context of COVID-19. That Interim Guidance dated 7th April, 2020 was issued by the WHO and has also not been revised.\n\nThen, Sir, I would like to quote from the famous medical journal \u201cThe Lancet\u201d, which talks in its Editorial about \"Advancing racial and ethnic equity in health\".\n\n\u201cRacism is a public health emergency of global concern.\u201d\n\n\"\u2026 an acknowledgment of racism and its harms - hatred, intolerance, and discrimination kill. These issues are as pervasive in medicine, medical science, and global health as in society. Today, The Lancet publishes a special issue bringing together the strongest evidence and analysis on advancing racial and ethnic equity in science, medicine, and health\u2026\u201d\n\nFinally, they say, I quote:\n\n\"Racism is not only about the health of particular persecuted or excluded groups - it inflicts a collective trauma on us all. The positive corollary of this fact is that lessening inequities and restoring justice can bring healing to society as a whole.\""
